# Docusaurus content & navigation

Read the always-on `docs-pakem.mdc` for page shape, `docs-sync.mdc` for when a page must change, and `docs-tone.mdc` for published voice. This file owns the mechanics of the site itself.

## Front matter

Every page under `docs/` opens with all four keys:

```yaml
---
title: Sharing a file
description: One sentence a search engine and a preview card can use.
sidebar_label: Sharing
sidebar_position: 3
---
```

- `sidebar_position` orders siblings inside one folder. Nested folders keep their own `_category_.json` for the label and position; the **top-level** grouping lives in `sidebars.ts`, not in a `_category_.json`, so there is one place to look.
- No `slug:` — the URL is the file path, and changing it breaks every link into the page.

## Navigation

- `sidebars.ts` is hand-grouped (Products · Core · Project); sub-folders are `{type: 'autogenerated', dirName: '<folder>'}`, so a new page inside one is picked up without editing the file.
- Every `docId` and `to:` in `docusaurus.config.ts` (navbar, footer) must resolve — `onBrokenLinks: 'throw'` fails the build otherwise.
- A page that is not reachable from the sidebar is an orphan; `npm run check:docs` fails on it.
- A new product gets: `docs/{kebab}/about.md`, a `sidebars.ts` category under Products, navbar + footer entries, and a `docs-coverage.json` entry.

## Content

- **English only.** Published copy is the customer's manual, not a translation surface. The site's locale set is `['en']` by design — the product's seven locales (`en`, `id`, `ja`, `ko`, `zh_CN`, `ar`, `ru`) are a different surface and do not apply here. Adding a site locale is a deliberate configuration decision, not an automatic mirror.
- **Match shipped behavior.** Use the real UI path (`/apps/profile/password`), the real plan names, the real locale list. Never invent a feature, a limit, or an SLA.
- Write to the reader: second person, present tense, imperative for steps. A heading is a stable label, not a sentence.
- Admonitions (`:::tip`, `:::info`, `:::warning`, `:::note`) are for a real gotcha; never decorate with them.
- Images and other assets live under `static/img/**` and are referenced by absolute path (`/img/...`).

## Gates

```sh
npm run check:docs
npm run typecheck
npm run build
```
